## Commands

The environment is managed with uv (Python {{PYTHON_VERSION}}, pinned in `.python-version`). The package is `src/{{PACKAGE}}`.

```bash
uv sync                                  # create/update .venv from uv.lock
uv add <pkg>  /  uv add --dev <pkg>      # add a dependency (never pip install)
uv run pytest                            # run all tests (testpaths = tests/)
uv run pytest tests/test_x.py::test_name # run a single test
uv run ruff check . --fix                # lint (rules: E,F,I,B,UP,NPY; line length 100)
uv run ruff format .                     # format

uv run jupytext --sync --execute notebooks/NN_name.py  # sync .py → .ipynb and re-run it in a fresh kernel
uv run pytest --nbmake notebooks/        # execute every notebook as a test (does not write outputs)
uv run jupyter lab                       # interactive use; kernel "python3" is the project .venv
```

## Code layout: package + notebooks

The code is presented as Jupyter notebooks, backed by a tested package:
- **`src/{{PACKAGE}}/`**: the reusable maths (the method, plus synthetic data generation), unit-tested in `tests/`.
  Notebooks import from it. They never redefine its functions or copy them between notebooks.
- **`notebooks/NN_name.ipynb`**: numbered narrative notebooks that walk through the paper section by section with figures
  ({{NOTEBOOK_PLAN}}). Outputs **are committed**, because the figures are the reproduction results.
- Every notebook is **paired by jupytext** with `notebooks/NN_name.py` (percent format; see `[tool.jupytext]` in pyproject).
  **Edit the `.py` file, never the `.ipynb` JSON**, then run `jupytext --sync --execute` on it. The `.py` file is what ruff lints
  (`*.ipynb` is excluded) and what reviewers read. To view rendered figures, read the `.ipynb`.
- `tests/test_notebooks.py` fails if a pair is out of sync or if outputs don't come from one top-to-bottom run. It cannot detect stale outputs
  after a `--sync` without `--execute`, so always use `--execute`.

